ressed Start again and held Right ~130 frames to World 1-1's first Goomba. list_sprites then decoded the Goomba's 6-entry OAM group (palette 7, OAM slots 52-57) as tiles $FC,$FC,$71,$65,$73,$72 - i.e. CHR tile 101 ($65) now occupies the slot where CHR tile 112 ($70) sat in the unedited Goomba ($FC,$FC,$71,$70,$73,$72) - and the screenshot shows the Goomba at screen ~(122,185)-(137,208) drawn with that different tile. undo_edit (ledger seq 1) restored the byte to $70. This proves prgRom 0x6794 supplies the Goomba's upper body tile. Caveat on drawing order: the game reverses the tile order with OAM horizontal flips for a left-facing Goomba, but the table bytes are always 70 71 72 73.","rom_origins":[{"mem":"prgRom","offset":26430,"length":260,"notes":"Enemy/sprite metasprite tile-id table, CPU $E73E-$E841 (after the enemy code ending JMP $EB64 at $E73B, before the numeric data at $E842). FC-padded runs of 8x8 sprite tile ids from pattern table $0000; Goomba run 70 71 72 73 at 0x6794 (entry FC FC 70 71 72 73 at 0x6792)."}]}}
