{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's the result of sheet 2's task.\n\n## The table\n**PRG ROM enemy/sprite metasprite tile‑id table, prgRom `0x673E–0x6841`** (CPU `$E73E–$E841`, 260 bytes) — the data block between the enemy code ending `JMP $EB64` at `$E73B` and the numeric data at `$E842`.\n\n- It is a list of 8×8 sprite‑pattern‑table (`$0000`) tile ids in $FC‑padded runs — one run per enemy/sprite form: the **red Koopa** `A5 A6 A7 A8 A9`, koopa/shell runs `6E 6E 6F 6F`, `6D 6D 6F 6F`, `6F 6F 6E 6E`, and `$BF–$EE` ids later in the block.\n- **Goomba's entry:** `FC FC 70 71 72 73` at **`0x6792–0x6797`** (the four body tiles `70 71 72 73` at `0x6794–0x6797`) — the top row `$70,$71` and bottom row `$72,$73` of its 2×2 body, with the two `$FC` blank fillers in front.\n\n## Checking the hit\n`search_memory prgRom \"70 71 72 73\"` returned a **single** hit at `0x6794` (`\"72 73\"` also single, at `0x6796`). The table has no direct absolute operand in the 32 KiB PRG (no `94 E7` / `92 E7` / `8C E7`; the lone `90 E7` at `0x6121` is a `BCC` operand), and a per‑frame read trace on `$E794` caught nothing — so the engine reads it indirectly/spawn‑time rather than per frame. The hit is confirmed by the write proof below.\n\n## Proof (all in hack `eval-sheet2-c`)\n- `new_hack eval-sheet2-c` → `use_hack eval-sheet2-c` (ledger empty, emulator bytes unchanged).\n- Ledgered `write_memory prgRom 0x6794 = $65` (was `$70`; `$65` is the round fireball/ball tile), with a reason. **ledger seq 1.**\n- `reset_emulator`, Start/Start, held Right ~130 frames to World 1‑1's first Goomba.\n- `list_sprites` decoded the Goomba's 6‑entry palette‑7 OAM group (slots 52‑57) as **`$FC,$FC,$71,$65,$73,$72`** — CHR tile 101 (`$65`) now sits in the slot where CHR tile 112 (`$70`) was in the unedited Goomba (`$FC,$FC,$71,$70,$73,$72`); the screenshot showed the Goomba at screen ≈(122,185)–(137,208) drawn with that different tile. (It faces left, so the game reverses the order with OAM H‑flips, but the table bytes are always `70 71 72 73`.)\n- `undo_edit seq 1` restored `$70` (ledger empty).\n\n## Persistence\n- `record_mapping` (note, id/name **\"enemy sprite layout table\"**) with the full notes, the Goomba entry, and `rom_origins` = `{mem: prgRom, offset: 26430 (0x673E), length: 260}`.\n- `promote_mappings` — saved to the shared mapping file.\n- `use_hack default` — back on the default hack, both ledgers empty, ROM bytes pristine."}
